  "notes": [
    "Regular -ER verb — follows standard endings in every tense, no exceptions.",
    "False friend warning: *pretender* does NOT usually mean \"to pretend\" (that's *fingir*) — it means to intend, attempt, or claim something.",
    "*Roberto pretende impresionar a la mujer.* (\"Roberto intends to impress the woman.\")",
    "*No pretendo ofenderte con esto.* (\"I don't intend to offend you with this.\")",
    "Related: *la pretensión* (intention/claim, noun), *fingir* (false-friend \"to pretend\"), *aspirar a* (synonym, \"to aspire to\")."
  ],
